      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know if we should by default exclude exonerated tests. I think the default behavior being more \"pure\" to the data source has value in keeping the skill versatile. I would turn this into --ignore-exonerated like --ignore-flaky.\n\nAlso, related but not actionable in this CL; we are at a bad spot in # of exonerated tests, especially in Linux and Windows :/ Exoneration causes flaky tests to be effectively disabled for CQ but cause reverts in CI, so tests shouldn\u0027t be permanently in this state; they should get fixed or disabled.",
